  <Description>&lt;h1&gt;
      AcordFormAttachment
    &lt;/h1&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;
      This route parses an Accord XML document and separates out individual 
      Base64 encoded attachments, saving them to individual files in an output 
      directory.
    &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;h2&gt;
      &lt;b&gt;Listener:&lt;/b&gt;
    &lt;/h2&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;
      &lt;b&gt;Sets a parameter, &amp;quot;guid&amp;quot;, that contains the TransRefGUID associated 
      with the document being processed. &lt;/b&gt;
    &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;ul&gt;
      &lt;li&gt;
        Programmable Listener
      &lt;/li&gt;
      &lt;li&gt;
        Inbound from Incoming-121-For-APS-Order
      &lt;/li&gt;
      &lt;li&gt;
        Processor: XPath Eval - set guid //ns:TransRefGUID (the unique ID 
        associated with the &lt;u&gt;entire&lt;/u&gt; document)
      &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;h2&gt;
      &lt;b&gt;Source Transform:&lt;/b&gt;
    &lt;/h2&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;
      &lt;b&gt;Executes XPath Forking upon each eval. of //ns:Attachment, the 
      enclosing tag of attachment data (if any)&lt;/b&gt;
    &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;ul&gt;
      &lt;li&gt;
        Format Profile:
      &lt;/li&gt;
      &lt;li&gt;
        No Transformation
      &lt;/li&gt;
      &lt;li&gt;
        Forking: XPath Fork on eval. of //ns:Attachment
      &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;h2&gt;
      &lt;b&gt;Route:&lt;/b&gt;
    &lt;/h2&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;
      Discard transaction if TransferEncodingTypeString is not base64 or if 
      the length of the attachment is 0.
    &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;h2&gt;
      &lt;b&gt;Target Transform:&lt;/b&gt;
    &lt;/h2&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;
      &lt;b&gt;Relay Target Transform&lt;/b&gt;
    &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;h2&gt;
      &lt;b&gt;Transport:&lt;/b&gt;
    &lt;/h2&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;
      &lt;b&gt;Sets the attributes fileName and fileExtension for use in the output 
      filename. Retrives the Base64 body of the attachment. Decodes the Base64 
      to ASCII for output file. Writes an output file for each transaction 
      containing an attachment.&lt;/b&gt;
    &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;ul&gt;
      &lt;li&gt;
        Processor1: XPath Eval. - fileName = 
        //accord:Description[substring-before(.,'.')], fileExtension = 
        //accord:Description[substring-after(.,'.')]
      &lt;/li&gt;
      &lt;li&gt;
        Processor2: Sets the body of the transaction to the XPath evaluation 
        //AttachmentData.
      &lt;/li&gt;
      &lt;li&gt;
        Processor3: Decodes the Base64 transaction body to an ASCII string.
      &lt;/li&gt;
      &lt;li&gt;
        Writes out a file that contains the decoded attachment data and sets 
        the file extension relative to the mimeType)
      &lt;/li&gt;
      &lt;li&gt;
        Target Filename: getAttribute('guid') - getAttribute('fileName') File 
        Extension: getAttribute('fileExtension')
      &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;/ul&gt;</Description>
</Route>

